## ## Retorno
## An owned hex string; release it with `banish`.
weave sha3_384 with data as string into string:
    return calling _hash_hex with ALG_SHA3_384 , data

## Returns the SHA3-512 digest of `data` as 128 lowercase hex characters.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the bytes to digest. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned hex string; release it with `banish`.
weave sha3_512 with data as string into string:
    return calling _hash_hex with ALG_SHA3_512 , data

## Returns the BLAKE2b digest of `data` as lowercase hex.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the bytes to digest. Borrowed.
## - `digest_size`: the digest length in bytes (default `64`, legal `1..64`).
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned hex string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling seal.blake2b with "hello"          # 128 hex characters
## calling seal.blake2b with "hello", 32      # 64 hex characters
## ```
weave blake2b with data as string , digest_size as int is 64 into string:
    if digest_size < 1 or digest_size > 64:
        return ""
    return calling _blake_hex with ALG_BLAKE2B , data , digest_size

## Returns the BLAKE2s digest of `data` as lowercase hex.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the bytes to digest. Borrowed.
## - `digest_size`: the digest length in bytes (default `32`, legal `1..32`).
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned hex string; release it with `banish`.
weave blake2s with data as string , digest_size as int is 32 into string:
    if digest_size < 1 or digest_size > 32:
        return ""
    return calling _blake_hex with ALG_BLAKE2S , data , digest_size

## BLAKE2 digest with an explicit digest size (private).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `alg`: `ALG_BLAKE2B` or `ALG_BLAKE2S`.
## - `data`: the bytes. Borrowed.
## - `digest_size`: the requested digest length in bytes.
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned hex string; release it with `banish`. The size travels to the engine
## as a one-byte `data` on the size-aware init opcode, because BLAKE2 mixes the
## requested output length into its parameter block before absorbing any input.
weave _blake_hex with alg as int , data as string , digest_size as int into string:
    var state as string is calling _blob_new with HASH_STATE_BYTES
    defer banish state
    var out as string is ""
    calling _blake2_op with OP_INIT_SIZE , alg , (sigil of state) , (chr digest_size) , (sigil of out)
    calling _blake2_op with OP_UPDATE , alg , (sigil of state) , data , (sigil of out)
    calling _blake2_op with OP_FINAL_HEX , alg , (sigil of state) , "" , (sigil of out)
    return out

## Returns the digest of the file at `path` under algorithm `alg` (private).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `alg`: an `ALG_*` id.
## - `path`: the file to read; streamed in 64 KiB chunks. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some hex` (owned) or `none` when the file cannot be read.
weave _engine_file_hex with alg as int , path as string into maybe string:
    if (calling _digest_len with alg) == 0:
        return maybe none
    var state as string is calling _blob_new with HASH_STATE_BYTES
    defer banish state
    var out as string is ""
    var status as int is 0
    if alg <= ALG_SHA384:
        set status is calling _sha2_op with OP_FILE_HEX , alg , (sigil of state) , path , (sigil of out)
    else if alg <= ALG_SHA3_512:
        set status is calling _sha3_op with OP_FILE_HEX , alg , (sigil of state) , path , (sigil of out)
    else:
        set status is calling _blake2_op with OP_FILE_HEX , alg , (sigil of state) , path , (sigil of out)
    if status != 0:
        return maybe none
    return some out

